<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoOperationMultiply</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Function to implement multiplication</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Operation.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">SilikoValue *SilikoOperationMultiply(int argc, SilikoValue **argv);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoOperationMultiply</function> function
calculates the product of the values passed in <varname>argv</varname> 
where <varname>argc</varname> is the number of values passed.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para><function>SilikoOperationMultiply</function> returns a pointer to
an object representing the result of the multiplication
operation.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Conformance</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoOperationMultiply</function> function conforms
to Siliko Core’s interface for pure functions and can be installed into
a <type>SilikoEngine</type> if wrapped with
<function>SilikoPureFunctionCreate</function>.</para>
</refsection>
